  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [raspie](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=raspie) [on June 27, 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4168259) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168269) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168526)\[–\]<br>\> Internet Explorer 6 normally ignores PNG transparency and displays a solid background colour.<br>\> With TinyPNG the background becomes transparent again. No workarounds!<br>Um, does anyone know how that works? Does IE6 natively support some kind of png transparency?<br>EDIT: ah, like that: [http://calendar.perfplanet.com/2010/png-that-works/#8bit+alp...](http://calendar.perfplanet.com/2010/png-that-works/#8bit+alpha) | |
  | |     |     |     |
