  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [lilyball](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=lilyball) [on June 27, 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4168220) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168446) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168352)\[–\]<br>The shadow on that compressed panda has visible artifacts. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [berkut](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=berkut) [on June 27, 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4169246) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168220) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168352)\[–\]<br>Yeah, it almost looks like a premultiply issue, but PNG should be non-premultiplied, so...<br>[http://imgur.com/6ovIu](http://imgur.com/6ovIu)<br>Also, the original has values in the RGB channels for pixels with no alpha that aren't visible (due to the alpha) but need to be compressed, so it's not a fair test (although both do to some degree - turquoise area around the bear), so the new one could be compressed even more. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [pornel](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=pornel) [on June 27, 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4169386) \| [root](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168220) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4169246) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168352)\[–\]<br>pngquant backing this service works in premultiplied RGBA colorspace (but with 32-bit floating point per gun).<br>However the distortion is merely a side-effect of reducing image to 256-colors (from 15k colors). | |
