  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [james33](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=james33) [on June 27, 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4169178) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4168352) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4169095)\[–\]<br>I've only tried one image so far, but the one I tried showed impressive results. I've always used [http://punypng.com](http://punypng.com/), which has always done a great job, but I just ran a file compressed down to 131kb in PunyPNG and TinyPNG took it down to 42kb! | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [nathos](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=nathos) [on June 27, 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4169095) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4169178) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4170279)\[–\]<br>For those looking for a desktop application with more options (for Mac at least), check out Image Alpha: [http://pngmini.com/](http://pngmini.com/)<br>(from the creator of the equally awesome ImageOptim: [http://imageoptim.com/](http://imageoptim.com/)) | |
