  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [gcr](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=gcr) [on June 28, 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4169971) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4170279) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4167964#4170232)\[–\]<br>PNG compresses "exact" gradients pretty well. I'd be interested in a tool that not only reduces colors (what this one is doing), but also smooths gradient-like segments of the image to comrpess better. | |
